{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-lie-bracket","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Example","doco:Section"],"label":"ex:q-lie-bracket","kind":"example","title":"$q$-Deformed Lie bracket","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-lie-bracket"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-reeb","tags":["lie-bracket","archimedean"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.qLieBracket","text":"q-lie-bracket.md","leanSource":"q-lie-bracket.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"ex:q-lie-bracket\"></a><p>In the archimedean realisation, the categorical Reeb derivation induces the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformed Lie bracket on vector fields <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V, W \\in \\mathfrak{X}(M)</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  [V, W]_q = q^{-1}[V, W] + (1 - q^{-1})\\bigl(\\varTheta(V)\\mathcal{L}_\\xi W - \\varTheta(W)\\mathcal{L}_\\xi V\\bigr).</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-lie-bracket.md","heading":"Example","number":"4.20.2","page":"b/ex-q-lie-bracket","qa":{"counts":{"pass":66,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":8,"unknown":0,"stale":48},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.qLieBracket","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-lie-bracket.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
